linda (docs): opened PR to consolidate several small docs fixes: refresh streaming snippets across languages, add a tiny retry/backoff example, clarify cursor pagination semantics, and repair the dead internal link to the retry guide. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/889

harry (eng): thanks — will review python + ts. are we changing any public API surface or purely editorial?

yasmin (sdk): purely editorial. we want idiomatic names (stream_generate for py; streamGenerate for ts/go) and to include one-line caveats about short-output buffering. i'll take Go and scan TS for accuracy.

linda (docs): correct — no behavioural changes. also adding a 1-iteration examples harness so CI can catch streaming regressions. pasted the proposed snippets below for quick eyeballs.

linda (docs): ```python
# python streaming + retry (minimal for CI)
from redwood import Client
import asyncio
client = Client()
async def sample_once():
    async for chunk in client.stream_generate("Summarize this paragraph.", max_tokens=80, retry_policy={"backoff":"exponential","max_retries":2}):
        print(chunk.text)
        break
asyncio.run(sample_once())
```

linda (docs): ```ts
// typescript streaming (minimal)
const s = client.streamGenerate({ prompt: 'Summarize this paragraph.', maxTokens: 80 });
for await (const c of s) {
  console.log(c.text);
  break;
}
// note: transport may coalesce very short outputs; boundaries are approximate
```

linda (docs): ```go
// go: cursor pagination minimal
ctx := context.Background()
iter := client.ListEmbeddings(ctx, &redwood.ListEmbeddingsRequest{PageSize: 25})
if iter.Next() {
    _ = iter.Item()
}
if err := iter.Err(); err != nil {
    // report / retry
}
// comment: next_cursor is empty at EOF; honor context cancellation to stop streaming
```

tom (qa): can we wire the harness into the docs preview CI as an optional check? it should run each sample once and exit nonzero only on exceptions. async generators have been flaky in CI before.

yasmin (sdk): will add a tiny script in the PR that runs the three examples with a short timeout. also added a Go comment about honoring ctx.Done() to cancel long-running paginated workloads.

harry (eng): small nit: the retry link in the current draft pointed at /retries; canonical path is /retry-guides. pls update to avoid the 404.

linda (docs): fixed the link and added a short "Streaming caveats" subsection about KV-cache interaction and prefix caching with streaming responses.

yasmin (sdk): ran the Go example against the internal test model — works. i clarified the cursor example to show a sample comment for next_cursor handling. pushed one tiny comment tweak.

tom (qa): harness ran on the preview build; passed. added a one-line caution in TS about buffering differences on very short prompts.

